From c0334f4a8095a3bb79983ef7fac52ff033da1bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tianling Shen <cnsztl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:00:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dhcpv6: refresh bindings after on-link prefix changes

Learning a new RA prefix currently forces the client through EXIT,
releasing valid leases and restarting server discovery even when it
remains on the same link. This causes unnecessary lease churn and can
trigger PPP teardown on affected access networks.

Queue significant on-link prefix changes independently of restart
signals and consume existing replies before starting a refresh at a
bound safe point. Preserve active acquisition and maintenance
exchanges, including an already accepted Reconfigure, and rate-limit
RA-triggered attempts to one every 30 seconds.

Use Renew for valid delegated prefixes, Confirm for address-only
bindings and Information-request for information-only configuration,
as described in RFC 9915 section 18.2.12. Preserve stateless
rediscovery when the original configuration requests IAs.

Track on-link PIOs separately from SLAAC addresses so L-only and
non-/64 prefixes, equal-count prefix replacements and explicit
deprecation are detected on both regular and point-to-point links.
Repeated advertisements do not trigger another refresh.

Handle Confirm replies without updating the server binding,
configuration or lease lifetimes. Accept Success from any server, wait
through the confirmation window before acting on NotOnLink and retain
leases if no server responds. Resume lease timers from aged IA data
without double-counting elapsed time.

Fixes: 038407eca8a4 ("dhcpv6: restart DHCPv6 on receipt of RA containing a new prefix")
Signed-off-by: Tianling Shen <cnsztl@gmail.com>
